BT /F2 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 568.69 Td (Q: What do I get for driving 120 km to a client in my own car?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 554.29 Td (A: 12 mil at SEK 30 is SEK 360, of which SEK 300 is tax-free and SEK 60 is paid as taxable salary.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 531.89 Td (Q: Is the Group's rate of EUR 0.30 per km used in Sweden?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 517.49 Td (A: No. In Sweden this addendum applies, so the rate is SEK 30 per mil.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 495.09 Td (Q: I travel to Gothenburg on Monday at 08:00 and come back Tuesday at 17:00. What per diem) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 480.69 Td (do I get?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 466.29 Td (A: Monday is a full day \(SEK 300\) because you leave before 12:00, and Tuesday is a half day \(SEK) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 451.89 Td (150\) because you are back before 19:00 - SEK 450 in total, less any meals paid for.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 429.49 Td (Q: The hotel included breakfast. Does that matter?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.40 Tf 0.120 0.130 0.150 rg 58.00 415.09 Td (A: Yes. A breakfast that is paid for reduces that day's per diem by 20%.) Tj ET
